statement:
Let $k$ be algebraically closed, $C/k$ a smooth proper connected curve of genus $g$, $P\in C(k)$, and let $\underline{\operatorname{Pic}}_{C/k}=\coprod_d\underline{\operatorname{Pic}}^d_{C/k}$ be as in [det-picard-main-degree]. Let $H_g$ be a scheme representing $\operatorname{Hilb}^g_{C/k}$ as in [thm-pc-hilb-curves]. Then:

1. $\underline{\operatorname{Pic}}_{C/k}$ is locally of finite type, smooth of pure dimension $g$ and separated over $k$;
1. the Abel map $\alpha:H_g\to\underline{\operatorname{Pic}}^g_{C/k}$, $D\mapsto\mathcal O_C(D)$ (normalized along $P$), is surjective;
1. every $\underline{\operatorname{Pic}}^d_{C/k}$ is a smooth proper geometrically irreducible (in particular geometrically connected) variety of dimension $g$.
